// PREDICATED SORT chain: C = B where inC, where B = A where inB. A refined sort may
// refine another refined sort. The base-sort resolver walks the refinement chain to the root
// A; the qualifiers accumulate into ONE CONJOINED guard — so `forall c: C; P(c)` desugars to
// `forall c: A; (inC(c) and inB(c)) -> P(c)` (child qualifier first, the accumulation order).
// The conjunction is the CANONICAL relativization shape: it is exactly what the kernel's
// guarded-fix `forall_intro` derives, so statements, fix blocks, and transfers all agree.
sort A
pred inB(a: A)
sort B = A where inB
pred inC(b: B)              // a pred over the REFINED B (its base sort is A)
sort C = B where inC

pred P(a: A)

axiom pForC: forall c: A; (inC(c) and inB(c)) -> P(c)

theorem chainDesugars: forall c: C; P(c)
proof
  @conclusion |
    forall c: C; P(c)
    [by cite pForC]
qed
